{
  "id": "03-clone-graph",
  "title": "Clone Graph",
  "track": "Graphs",
  "difficulty": "medium",
  "topics": [
    "graphs"
  ],
  "source": "canonical Clone Graph concept; description, examples, and tests re-authored",
  "description": "The input is the first node of a connected graph; each node holds a value and a list of neighbors, values are unique, and the links may form cycles. Return a deep copy of the graph: fresh nodes with the same values and the same neighbor structure, sharing nothing with the original. An input of None returns None. The GraphNode class is provided in the starter code.",
  "constraints": [
    "1 <= number of nodes <= 2000",
    "node values are unique integers from 1 to the node count",
    "the graph is connected"
  ],
  "parameters": [
    "node"
  ],
  "functionName": "clone_graph",
  "starterCode": "class GraphNode:\n    def __init__(self, value=0):\n        self.value = value\n        self.neighbors = []\n\ndef clone_graph(node):\n    # node has .value and .neighbors; return a deep copy of the graph.\n    ...\n",
  "prepareCode": "class GraphNode:\n    def __init__(self, value=0):\n        self.value = value\n        self.neighbors = []\n\ndef build_graph(adj):\n    if not adj:\n        return None\n    nodes = {index + 1: GraphNode(index + 1) for index in range(len(adj))}\n    for index, neighbor_values in enumerate(adj):\n        for value in neighbor_values:\n            nodes[index + 1].neighbors.append(nodes[value])\n    return nodes[1]\n\ndef serialize(node):\n    if node is None:\n        return []\n    adjacency = {}\n    queue = [node]\n    seen = {node.value}\n    while queue:\n        current = queue.pop(0)\n        adjacency[current.value] = [neighbor.value for neighbor in current.neighbors]\n        for neighbor in current.neighbors:\n            if neighbor.value not in seen:\n                seen.add(neighbor.value)\n                queue.append(neighbor)\n    return [adjacency[value] for value in sorted(adjacency)]\n\ndef prepare(raw):\n    head = build_graph(raw[0])\n    def finish(result):\n        return serialize(result)\n    return [head], finish\n",
  "examples": [
    {
      "input": {
        "node": [
          [
            2
          ],
          [
            3
          ],
          [
            1
          ]
        ]
      },
      "output": [
        [
          2
        ],
        [
          3
        ],
        [
          1
        ]
      ],
      "explanation": "A three-node ring clones into a fresh three-node ring."
    },
    {
      "input": {
        "node": []
      },
      "output": [],
      "explanation": "An empty graph clones to an empty graph."
    }
  ],
  "hints": [
    "The clone of a node is easy; the trap is visiting the same node twice and cloning it twice.",
    "Keep one memo: original node in, clone out. A visited clone never gets rebuilt, only relinked.",
    "Breadth-first or depth-first, both work: for each original, build its clone, then append the clones of its neighbors as the neighbors list."
  ],
  "solution": "Traversal with a memo mapping each original node to its clone: build the clone on first visit, append it to the queue or stack, and wire neighbor clones as they become available. Every node and edge is processed once: O(V + E) time, O(V) space.",
  "solutionCode": "def clone_graph(node):\n    if node is None:\n        return None\n    clones = {node.value: GraphNode(node.value)}\n    queue = [node]\n    while queue:\n        current = queue.pop(0)\n        for neighbor in current.neighbors:\n            if neighbor.value not in clones:\n                clones[neighbor.value] = GraphNode(neighbor.value)\n                queue.append(neighbor)\n            clones[current.value].neighbors.append(clones[neighbor.value])\n    return clones[node.value]\n",
  "bruteForceCode": "def clone_graph(node):\n    if node is None:\n        return None\n    originals = []\n    stack = [node]\n    while stack:\n        current = stack.pop()\n        if not any(current is seen for seen in originals):\n            originals.append(current)\n            stack.extend(current.neighbors)\n    clones = [GraphNode(original.value) for original in originals]\n    for index, original in enumerate(originals):\n        for neighbor in original.neighbors:\n            for position, seen in enumerate(originals):\n                if seen is neighbor:\n                    clones[index].neighbors.append(clones[position])\n                    break\n    for clone in clones:\n        if clone.value == node.value:\n            return clone\n    return None\n",
  "failureHint": "hidden tests include a single node, self-loops in the neighbor lists, and rings",
  "expectedComplexity": {
    "time": "O(V + E)",
    "space": "O(V)"
  },
